WEBVTT

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:20.790
Satowa...

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.410
Good...

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:39.660
I was looking for you...
hoping that you'd still be around here.

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:44.870
I heard your performance.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.410
I'm sorry...

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:52.700
What I did to you...

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:55.200
...can never be undone.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:59.250
It left a deep scar in your heart.

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:02.750
I know very well that it cannot be forgiven.

00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:08.500
So I don't have the right
to say this to you now... but...

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:14.620
...would you give me one more chance...
to properly face you?

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:20.250
S-So did my feelings...

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:22.660
...reach you this time?

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:28.540
Did I... do it right this time...?

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:30.580
Did they really reach--

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:51.790
Hozuki...!

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:53.540
I'm so happy for you!

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:54.660
You idiot!

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:56.160
Hey, Kota!

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:07.500
Seriously, Kota!
Why did you have to jump out like that?!

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:11.750
I'm sorry, Hozy... for ruining your
long-awaited reunion with your mom!

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:13.950
No, not at all...

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:15.620
Rather, I feel embarrassed.

00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:19.950
On top of having you look for her,
you saw me like that.

00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:21.000
I'm sorry.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:23.540
--What're you saying!
It's not embarrassing at all!

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:24.620
--U-Um, Hiro...
--What're you saying!
It's not embarrassing at all!

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:26.580
--How lively...
--U-Um, Hiro...
--What're you saying!
It's not embarrassing at all!

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:31.750
You really do resemble Hozuki.

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:34.950
If I remember correctly,
you played the 17-string...?

00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:37.160
Um, I'm Kudo.

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:40.450
I see... So you're the one...

00:04:40.450 --> 00:04:45.910
Well, you and the other boy played
the 17-string wonderfully.

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:49.830
Thank you for supporting my daughter.

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:53.200
Well...

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:57.040
It's more like she's been leading us
all this time... Ma'am.

00:04:57.040 --> 00:05:00.500
Leading and supporting are
two different things, right?

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:06.330
No wonder she cherishes
this club as well as all of you.

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:12.500
Thanks.

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:18.000
Oh, I'm so happy for her.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:18.950
Yep, yep.

00:05:18.950 --> 00:05:21.410
Well, all that running and crying
has made me parched.

00:05:21.410 --> 00:05:23.950
Chika! We'll play rock-paper-scissors
to decide who'll get us drinks!

00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:25.450
O-Okay.

00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:27.580
Grand Master.

00:05:27.580 --> 00:05:29.500
Akira...

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:33.200
Thank you for bringing me here.

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:35.950
Well, I'm sorry for taking you by force.

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:37.870
Okay, guys. Ready?!

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:39.450
--Rock, paper, scissors!
One, two, three! One, two, three!

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:44.120
--The kids in this club are just as you said.
--Rock, paper, scissors!
One, two, three! One, two, three!

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:45.370
They are.

00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:50.910
Damn! I suck at rock-paper-scissors
for some reason.

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:55.540
Whoa!

00:05:55.540 --> 00:05:58.750
Wh-What're you doing?!
How long have you been standing there?!

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:00.290
Hey, what're you looking at?!

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:02.830
What?! I'm not really looking at anything!

00:06:02.830 --> 00:06:04.870
I just came to buy some drinks.

00:06:09.660 --> 00:06:12.750
I bet you think you outdid us.

00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:14.080
Hm?

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:17.330
To see you're relaxing
and buying drinks like that...

00:06:17.330 --> 00:06:20.660
You must think that you guys are first place.

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:24.830
And you don't think you're first?

00:06:24.830 --> 00:06:30.580
Being in sync meant everything to me... to us.

00:06:30.580 --> 00:06:34.200
Bing in sync was supreme and beautiful...

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:38.250
That's what music meant to us.

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:40.620
But then...

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:43.750
I heard you guys' performance.

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:49.330
Now I feel like all that focus on
just being in sync... seems stupid.

00:06:51.250 --> 00:06:53.620
What're you saying?

00:06:53.620 --> 00:06:55.950
"<i>Just </i>being in sync"?

00:06:55.950 --> 00:06:58.620
It's not like that at all.

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:03.080
You guys played perfectly with that speed,
with that many people.

00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:07.120
I genuinely thought that was pretty cool.

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:12.830
But... we're still gonna win.

00:07:17.410 --> 00:07:20.950
I-I said...

00:07:20.950 --> 00:07:25.120
...you were not worthy to play
the koto with Satowa.

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:27.080
I take it back.

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:28.910
It pains me to say it...

00:07:28.910 --> 00:07:31.290
I don't even want to admit it...!

00:07:34.040 --> 00:07:38.200
But your performance today was... really good!

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:42.080
Damn straight!

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:50.410
He ticks me off! Don't people normally
say "thanks" in this situation?!

00:07:52.620 --> 00:07:58.790
We will announce the results
and hold the closing ceremony now.

00:07:58.790 --> 00:08:02.790
We request that the participating
schools return to the hall.

00:08:05.120 --> 00:08:08.790
Thank you all for your performance today.

00:08:08.790 --> 00:08:12.200
This year, we heard so many good performances

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:14.410
that we thought this <i>was </i>nationals.

00:08:14.410 --> 00:08:17.330
It made us judges very happy.
But at the same time,

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:22.080
it made it unprecedently
difficult for us to judge.

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:26.540
Well... only one school
can go to nationals, right?

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:28.540
Himesaka, Hakuto, and Tokise...

00:08:28.540 --> 00:08:31.790
They are all good enough
to have a shot in nationals.

00:08:31.790 --> 00:08:35.450
But if we have to choose one school...

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:38.950
...I feel Tokise... might be the one after all.

00:08:38.950 --> 00:08:43.330
Their skill level is most satisfactory,
and more than anything,

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:44.620
I've never been so moved

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:49.450
by a performance from high school
students before, to be honest.

00:08:49.450 --> 00:08:55.580
I was purely moved and thought,
"How wonderful music is."

00:08:55.580 --> 00:08:57.700
I disagree.

00:08:57.700 --> 00:09:01.120
People these days really
only play modern pieces.

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:04.660
It's true that they have beautiful melodies
and easy to understand motifs,

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:06.910
so it's easy for them to remain in your heart.

00:09:06.910 --> 00:09:12.250
But it's not that hard
to play that kind of piece.

00:09:12.250 --> 00:09:14.540
I recommend Hakuto.

00:09:14.540 --> 00:09:18.950
They should get high marks for their
selection of piece and performance.

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:21.040
What do you think, Mr. Wada?

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:26.660
Well... I was moved the most by Tokise, too.

00:09:26.660 --> 00:09:31.040
But considering that this is a competition,
I'd choose Himesaka.

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:35.000
Their skills and ability to be perfectly
in sync, I think, is worthy of first place.

00:09:37.830 --> 00:09:41.410
Mr. Matsunaga. What's your opinion?

00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:46.700
If it were possible, we would want
everyone to go nationals.

00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:49.330
We seriously thought so.

00:09:49.330 --> 00:09:53.450
However, things like competitions are cruel.

00:09:53.450 --> 00:10:00.620
We have to assign a rank to all of your
hard work and the resulting performances.

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:05.540
We have to choose one school
that can go to nationals.

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:08.910
Well then, I'm now going
to announce that school.

00:10:08.910 --> 00:10:12.700
I think this school is the only choice.

00:10:12.700 --> 00:10:16.410
They were clearly in a different league...

00:10:16.410 --> 00:10:18.870
...in terms of what we call music.

00:10:20.540 --> 00:10:24.160
I do get what Ms. Midoriyama means, too.

00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:26.870
But their excellent performance
wasn't due to the fact that

00:10:26.870 --> 00:10:30.450
it was the kind of piece
that people like to hear.

00:10:30.450 --> 00:10:35.120
A truly wonderful performance
can go beyond experts

00:10:35.120 --> 00:10:40.080
and reach those who don't know much about koto.

00:10:40.080 --> 00:10:43.200
Its heart can reach even those
who speak a different language

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:45.620
and live in a different culture.

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:50.580
I think we should properly shine a light
on a performance like that.

00:10:51.660 --> 00:10:56.120
The 32nd Kanagawa Qualifier for
Japan High School Music Competition.

00:10:56.120 --> 00:11:00.790
The school that receives first place
and goes to nationals is...

00:11:05.660 --> 00:11:09.080
...Kanagawa Prefectural Tokise High School.

00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:15.540
All right!

00:11:15.540 --> 00:11:17.290
Whoooa! Seriously?!

00:11:17.290 --> 00:11:18.750
Really?! Seriously?!

00:11:18.750 --> 00:11:22.000
H-Hozy! We're first place...?!

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:23.750
I-Is it true?!

00:11:23.750 --> 00:11:24.580
Is it true?!

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:25.790
Yes!

00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:28.370
--Isaki! They did it!

00:11:28.370 --> 00:11:31.200
--Nationals! They're going to nationals!
--Isaki! They did it!

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:33.250
This is incredible...

00:11:35.120 --> 00:11:36.410
Really...?!

00:11:36.410 --> 00:11:37.950
Nationals...?!

00:11:46.870 --> 00:11:49.580
It didn't... end here...

00:11:49.580 --> 00:11:51.370
We can keep on going...!

00:11:51.370 --> 00:11:53.250
Chika! We did it!

00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:54.700
Kudo!

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:14.540
We're all going to nationals!

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:19.500
"Congrats!"

00:12:20.120 --> 00:12:22.250
Hey, guys! Good job!

00:12:22.250 --> 00:12:23.950
Isaki! Tetsuki!

00:12:23.950 --> 00:12:25.790
Mashiro!

00:12:25.790 --> 00:12:28.290
Congrats on winning! You guys are amazing!

00:12:28.290 --> 00:12:30.870
It really was a good performance!

00:12:30.870 --> 00:12:36.000
You see that, Isaki? Just like you told me,
we snatched the ticket to--

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:38.250
Attaboy!

00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:41.000
You did a good job! Good boy!

00:12:42.410 --> 00:12:44.410
S-Stop it, you dummy!

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:46.500
Oh, don't be so shy!

00:12:46.500 --> 00:12:48.040
Good boy, good boy.

00:12:48.040 --> 00:12:50.250
Mashiro, you came, too, huh?

00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:54.910
Of course! I happened to sit next to Isaki,
so we came to know each other.

00:12:54.910 --> 00:12:56.870
Congratulations, Takezo!

00:12:56.870 --> 00:13:00.040
It's amazing! You're going to nationals!
It's just amazing!

00:13:00.040 --> 00:13:04.160
Thank you so much for such
a wonderful performance!

00:13:04.160 --> 00:13:06.330
Mashiro...

00:13:07.700 --> 00:13:10.000
Now we're done for the time being.

00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:13.870
You've had composure from
the start till the end, Mr. Takinami.

00:13:13.870 --> 00:13:15.540
That's incredible.

00:13:15.540 --> 00:13:19.540
You must be joking, right?
I've been nervous all this time.

00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:20.790
What?

00:13:20.790 --> 00:13:25.540
If by any chance they couldn't go
to nationals with that performance,

00:13:25.540 --> 00:13:28.370
it'd be because of my arrangement of the piece.

00:13:28.370 --> 00:13:29.830
Th-That's not...

00:13:29.830 --> 00:13:35.750
Pieces that are easy to listen
to sometimes aren't taken seriously.

00:13:35.750 --> 00:13:38.200
So I'm relieved from the bottom of my heart now.

00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:44.330
This is the first time I've heard
you express any sort of worry.

00:13:44.330 --> 00:13:45.870
Why do you look happy?

00:13:45.870 --> 00:13:47.330
What? Well, I didn't mean--

00:13:47.330 --> 00:13:48.790
Akira!

00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:57.250
Ah... So... he came...

00:13:58.750 --> 00:14:00.790
You did it! You guys're going to nationals!

00:14:00.790 --> 00:14:03.950
Seriously, I was moved to tears
while listening to the performance!

00:14:03.950 --> 00:14:08.500
They're amazing, as can be expected
considering who their teacher is!

00:14:08.500 --> 00:14:11.700
What am I gonna do? It was so sudden
that I don't know what to say...

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:14.870
Excuse me! Are you Tokise High School's teacher?

00:14:14.870 --> 00:14:18.450
I'm Akira's older brother!
Thank you for being good to my sister!

00:14:18.450 --> 00:14:22.200
Oh, hello. I'm Takinami,
the advisor for the club.

00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:24.290
She's the one who's been good to us.

00:14:24.290 --> 00:14:26.040
You are Miss Aki's brother?!

00:14:26.040 --> 00:14:27.620
Whoa! You resemble her!

00:14:27.620 --> 00:14:29.910
Well, I was surprised when you performed,

00:14:29.910 --> 00:14:33.540
but there really are many boys!
It seems like a lot of fun!

00:14:33.540 --> 00:14:37.000
Yep! It's fun! Miss Aki is a
super tough teacher, though.

00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:37.830
Hey!

00:14:37.830 --> 00:14:40.040
Oh? So she's tough, huh?

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:42.500
M-My lessons aren't particularly tough.

00:14:42.500 --> 00:14:47.000
But... if it wasn't Miss Akira who taught us,

00:14:47.000 --> 00:14:50.450
I don't think we would've gotten
the ticket to nationals.

00:14:50.450 --> 00:14:53.040
Thank you, Miss Akira.

00:14:53.040 --> 00:14:55.790
Yep, yep. I'm glad it was you, Miss Aki.

00:14:55.790 --> 00:14:57.040
Yeah!

00:15:00.620 --> 00:15:02.200
Hey, Miss Akira's brother?!

00:15:02.200 --> 00:15:04.160
I'm giving you a hug for Akira!

00:15:04.160 --> 00:15:05.410
What?!

00:15:05.410 --> 00:15:07.580
I want a hug from <i>her</i>.

00:15:07.580 --> 00:15:09.750
No way! I won't allow it!

00:15:09.750 --> 00:15:14.910
Your performance was innocent,
earnest, gentle, and warm...

00:15:14.910 --> 00:15:19.830
I could tell from your sound
that you really like the koto.

00:15:19.830 --> 00:15:23.830
Akira. Thanks for inviting me today.

00:15:23.830 --> 00:15:28.410
I was really glad to hear your current sound.

00:15:33.830 --> 00:15:37.410
Thank you... big brother...

00:15:47.040 --> 00:15:48.750
Oh, my dear little sister!

00:15:48.750 --> 00:15:50.700
Hey! Stop it!

00:15:51.450 --> 00:15:54.870
Kazusa. We have to get going.

00:15:54.870 --> 00:15:56.040
Kazu--

00:15:58.040 --> 00:16:00.620
I somehow knew...

00:16:00.620 --> 00:16:03.660
...from the moment I heard
Tokise's performance...

00:16:03.660 --> 00:16:08.910
He had faith in their sound
all the way till the end.

00:16:08.910 --> 00:16:11.870
But I...

00:16:11.870 --> 00:16:14.500
Don't cry! Don't cry! Don't cry!

00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:18.910
I don't have... the right to cry.

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:21.870
Hey. Just how long are you
gonna stay there like that?

00:16:21.870 --> 00:16:24.200
You're not the only one who feels--

00:16:26.200 --> 00:16:28.080
Kazusa.

00:16:28.080 --> 00:16:31.750
Let's play together at nationals for sure!

00:16:31.750 --> 00:16:34.200
--Hey, Kazu--
--I'm sorry!

00:16:34.200 --> 00:16:37.450
I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

00:16:37.450 --> 00:16:39.370
I'm sorry. I'm sorry!

00:16:39.370 --> 00:16:41.700
I'm sorry. I'm sorr--

00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:44.540
What're you apologizing for?

00:16:44.540 --> 00:16:47.370
There's not one single reason
to apologize, right?

00:16:47.370 --> 00:16:51.000
You gave such a wonderful performance.

00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:57.500
I'd like to thank you all for trying
so hard for us support members.

00:16:57.500 --> 00:17:01.750
It's okay. You can start again from here.

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:12.580
You can start building up again from here.

00:17:12.580 --> 00:17:14.700
Guys... I'm sorry.

00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:17.830
You practiced so hard...

00:17:17.830 --> 00:17:20.750
...but I wasn't good enough. I'm really sorry.

00:17:20.750 --> 00:17:22.200
Hold on a sec!

00:17:22.200 --> 00:17:26.290
Stop it. Why are <i>you </i>apologizing?

00:17:26.290 --> 00:17:28.870
Rather, <i>we </i>have to apologize.

00:17:28.870 --> 00:17:32.250
We said we'd get the ticket to
nationals as a farewell gift for you.

00:17:32.250 --> 00:17:34.200
We're sorry that we couldn't make it happen.

00:17:34.200 --> 00:17:36.080
What're you saying?!

00:17:36.080 --> 00:17:39.790
You guys played my piece so wonderfully!

00:17:39.790 --> 00:17:43.160
That alone made me really happy!

00:17:43.160 --> 00:17:46.580
So all I feel is appreciation for you.

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:50.790
It's just that if I had been
more of an expert in music...

00:17:53.750 --> 00:17:57.250
M-Mio?! What?! What's wrong?!

00:17:57.250 --> 00:18:01.790
I was going to win today.

00:18:01.790 --> 00:18:03.580
I wanted to win...

00:18:03.580 --> 00:18:06.700
...because for Mr. Yamamoto,
Club President, and others...

00:18:06.700 --> 00:18:09.660
...this is the last day.

00:18:09.660 --> 00:18:15.160
If I had become able to perform
like today long before,

00:18:15.160 --> 00:18:18.580
things might've turned out differently.

00:18:18.580 --> 00:18:22.580
Everyone... might've been laughing right now.

00:18:25.410 --> 00:18:27.910
I'm sorry.

00:18:27.910 --> 00:18:30.290
Hey, stop it.

00:18:30.290 --> 00:18:32.450
If we're talking blame, we've been depending

00:18:32.450 --> 00:18:35.580
on your performance all this time
even though you're a first year.

00:18:35.580 --> 00:18:37.790
How can we apologize?!

00:18:41.450 --> 00:18:43.790
Everyone! I forbid you to apologize!

00:18:43.790 --> 00:18:45.750
I won't apologize anymore, either.

00:18:45.750 --> 00:18:48.250
What exactly do you need to apologize for?!

00:18:48.250 --> 00:18:52.160
It was the best, top-level performance
you've ever given!

00:18:52.160 --> 00:18:55.750
I'll be proud of your performance
today for the rest of my life!

00:18:57.160 --> 00:19:02.290
When I saw... your sheet music
for the first time...

00:19:02.290 --> 00:19:06.540
...it looked like a starry sky
and I thought it was pretty.

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:10.830
I like the pieces you create.

00:19:10.830 --> 00:19:13.410
I'm glad that I was able to play them.

00:19:18.370 --> 00:19:20.040
Thank you.

00:19:23.450 --> 00:19:26.120
We gotta get going. You got everything?

00:19:26.120 --> 00:19:27.750
Yep.

00:19:40.830 --> 00:19:43.500
Tokise High School!

00:19:43.500 --> 00:19:45.790
Hey, Kazusa?

00:19:45.790 --> 00:19:48.290
Make sure you win!

00:19:48.290 --> 00:19:51.080
You're going to nationals after beating us!

00:19:51.080 --> 00:19:53.540
So make sure you win first place!

00:19:53.540 --> 00:19:55.750
Or I won't forgive you!

00:19:55.750 --> 00:19:58.330
Of course we will!

00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:12.200
That was a heck of a way to root for you guys.

00:20:12.200 --> 00:20:13.250
Whoa!

00:20:13.250 --> 00:20:14.910
Congrats on winning first place.

00:20:14.910 --> 00:20:17.160
It's upsetting that we lost, but...

00:20:17.160 --> 00:20:19.660
...good luck with nationals.

00:20:21.870 --> 00:20:26.330
Thus... with much joy and heartbreak...

00:20:26.330 --> 00:20:29.750
...the Kanagawa Qualifier came to an end.

